```text
The unit tests instantiate the Socket network implementation inside one test
process, using local listener/connector objects and threads. They allocate host
vectors, exercise asynchronous send/receive/test progress, and apply a
test-owned timeout. They validate the implementation's local control flow and
payload correctness.

They are not a two-host, two-gfx1151, Ethernet-over-USB4 integration test.
```
